---
// Required on a live site alongside /privacy. Plain terms, matching what the
// pricing page actually says. Nothing here may contradict src/data/site.ts.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, pricing } from '../data/site';
const updated = '24 August 2026';
---
<Base
  title="Terms"
  description={`The terms ${site.legalName} works under: what the build includes, how payment works, who owns what, and how to stop.`}
  path="/terms"
>
  <section class="section legal">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow label">
        <span>Terms</span>
        <span class="head-dim">&middot; Updated {updated}</span>
      </p>
      <h1>Terms</h1>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="short">
          Short version: {pricing.build.amount} for the standard build, half to start and
          half when you are happy. You own the site and the domain. Everything ongoing is
          month to month and you can stop whenever you like.
        </p>

        <h2>Who you are dealing with</h2>
        <p>
          {site.legalName}, run by {site.owner}, based in {site.base}. Contact details are
          in the footer of every page.
        </p>

        <h2>The demo</h2>
        <p>
          The free demo is free. You do not pay for it, you are not committed by asking for
          it, and if you do not want to go ahead that is the end of it. The demo stays up
          while we are talking and I take it down afterwards. It is not indexed by search
          engines and it is not a live site.
        </p>

        <h2>What the build costs</h2>
        <p>
          The standard build is {pricing.build.amount}. {pricing.build.terms} The first half
          starts the work, the second is due when you have reviewed it and you are happy for
          it to go live. {pricing.build.scopeNote}
        </p>
        <p>
          If the job turns out to be bigger than the standard build, I will tell you the
          number before I start it, not after.
        </p>

        <h2>Ongoing costs</h2>
        <p>
          Hosting and security is {pricing.hosting.amount}{pricing.hosting.per} and starts
          the day the site goes live. The Growth plan
          is {pricing.growth.amount}{pricing.growth.per} and includes hosting and security,
          so it replaces that cost rather than adding to it. Both are month to month with
          no lock-in and no minimum term. Give me a month's notice to stop.
        </p>

        <h2>What you have to do</h2>
        <p>
          Send me the photos, the details of your services and areas, and any licence or
          insurance information you want shown. I will chase you once or twice, but a build
          cannot finish without them, and a job that goes quiet for more than 60 days gets
          paused until you come back to it.
        </p>

        <h2>Who owns what</h2>
        <p>
          You own the domain, the content and the finished site. Once the build is paid for
          it is yours, and if you ever want to move it somewhere else you can take it with
          you. Photos and text you give me stay yours, and you are confirming you have the
          right to use them.
        </p>

        <h2>What I will not do</h2>
        <p>
          I will not invent reviews, licence numbers, ABNs, insurance claims or awards. If
          you cannot substantiate something, it does not go on your site. This protects you
          more than it protects me.
        </p>

        <h2>What I cannot promise</h2>
        <p>
          I cannot promise a Google position, a number of enquiries or a volume of work.
          Nobody honest can, because Google decides rankings and your market decides the
          rest. What I do promise is that the site is built properly, the technical
          groundwork is done, and on the Growth plan I keep working on it.
        </p>

        <h2>If something goes wrong</h2>
        <p>
          Tell me. Most things are a five minute fix and I would rather hear about it than
          have you sitting on it. Nothing here limits any rights you have under Australian
          Consumer Law.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>Last updated {updated}. If these change, the date changes with them.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose { max-width: 68ch; }
  .prose h2 {
    font-variation-settings: 'wdth' 110, 'wght' 650;
    font-size: clamp(19px, 2vw, 23px); letter-spacing: -.012em;
    margin: 36px 0 12px;
  }
  .prose p { color: var(--on-light-soft); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .short {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--amber); padding: 14px 18px;
    background: var(--linen); color: var(--ink) !important; font-size: 16px;
  }
</style>
